@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/Graphs/bipartite_graph_reconstruction_conjecture_2.lean
@decl Conjecture2
-- L4DEL: title: Let G = (U ⊔ V, E) be a finite simple bipartite graph with |U| = u, |V| = v, n = u + v ≥ 3
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let G = (U ⊔ V, E) be a finite simple bipartite graph with |U| = u, |V| = v, n = u + v ≥ 3. Assume: 1. G is 2-connected. 2. G is not a regular graph (the degree sequence is non-constant on U ⊔ V) 3. All vertex types are pairwise distinct Then deck(G) determines G uniquely up to bipartite isomorphism.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own leading source comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

