@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/Optimization/LastIterateConvergence.lean
@decl Arxiv.«1905.10899».last_iterate_convergence
-- L4DEL: title: The last-iterate convergence of Anchored Simultaneous Gradient Descent (SimGD-A) with parameter $p = 1/2$
-- L4DEL: intuition: The last-iterate convergence of Anchored Simultaneous Gradient Descent (SimGD-A) with parameter $p = 1/2$. This theorem corresponds to the critical boundary case of Theorem 3 in arXiv:1905.10899, where the step size $\alpha_t$ and anchoring coefficient $\beta_t$ are set to achieve an $O(1/T)$ convergence rate on the squared norm of the operator. While Theorem 3 in the paper is formally stated for $p \in (1/2, 1)$, the "Further discussion" in Section 4.2 identifies $p = 1/2$ as the theoretical limit of stability and discretization. A DeepMind prover agent was able to proof that convergence holds for $p = 1/2$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file APNOutputs/AICollaborator/Optimization/LastIterateConvergence.lean
@decl Arxiv.«1905.10899».step
-- L4DEL: title: Anchored Simultaneous Gradient Descent z_{t+1} = z_t - α_t * G(z_t) + β_t * (z_0 - z_t)
-- L4DEL: intuition: Anchored Simultaneous Gradient Descent z_{t+1} = z_t - α_t * G(z_t) + β_t * (z_0 - z_t)
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own leading source comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

